		<div class="flow">
			<h3>Why Filters Matter</h3>
			<p>
				Gun filters should always be used when available. Gun filters help strain the paint one more time before reaching the airless paint sprayer tip. Not choosing the
				proper filter can cause small bits of debris to flow through the gun and tip, causing not only tip clogs but also damage as well.
			</p>
			<p>The best way to choose the correct gun filter is to look at the orifice of the tip you are using:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Use a 100 Mesh Filter with tip orifice sizes .011&quot; through .015&quot;</li>
				<li>Use a 60 Mesh Filter with tip orifice sizes .017&quot; and  larger</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
